    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on two high-floor anchors against favorable matchups. **Josh Naylor** (66.07) and **Jose Caballero** (66.13) lead the way, both benefiting from soft matchups against right-handed pitching. **Jose Caballero** is a particularly intriguing play today; despite a dynamic platoon penalty, his score is propped up by a significant park factor (+16%) and a favorable matchup against the 4.78 xERA of Brandon Young. Meanwhile, **Josh Naylor** remains the cornerstone of our power production, maintaining a stable 66-point efficiency as he looks to exploit Peter Lambert\u2019s 4.16 xERA. While **Corbin Carroll** (59.75) falls just short of our \"Strong\" tier, he remains an essential start, primarily because his elite sprint speed makes him an irreplaceable contributor in our pursuit of stolen bases, even when facing a tough arm like Nathan Eovaldi.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today involved **Dalton Rushing** (39.48), who hovered right at the edge of our efficiency floor. The optimizer ultimately benched him in favor of **Gabriel Moreno** due to a brutal matchup against Trevor McDonald\u2019s 2.60 xERA. While **Dalton Rushing** provides value through his positional versatility, the penalty for facing such an elite arm effectively neutralized his upside for this slate. We are keeping a close watch on **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Cole Young**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Corbin Carroll**, as their scores are currently based on projected lineup spots; should any of them drop into the bottom third of the batting order, their efficiency scores will likely see a downward correction. \n\nWe are also monitoring the availability of **James Wood** and **Tyler Soderstrom**, both of whom are confirmed off for today\u2019s schedule, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active roster. While we have bench depth in **Alex Freeland**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Mickey Moniak**, 